 ## How the kanji combine
 
-[栄](../kanji/栄.md) suggests flourishing, while 養 concerns nourishing or sustaining. Together they name nourishment that supports living things. The on readings are エイ + ヨウ. This is a meaning aid, not a claim about the word's historical formation.
